Well... I don't think the point of this spoiler is to completely spoil you
on the whole game -- presumably you can figure out that dragon scales come
from dragons ;)  Quite a few of the other suggestions you made are along
the same vein -- good to note in some spoiler, but probably would just
clutter up this one.

Remember this spoiler is to give you suggestions, remind you to wish for
fixed / greased, and let you copy/paste proper spellings.  The purpose is
not to give you every possible wish, or tell you where every possible item
comes from.  You make similar suggestions later on -- "note that you can
polypile for this" and such.  I figure everybody should know that, yes,
you *can* polypile or wish for almost all of these things; that's not the
point.  The point is that you have a wish NOW that you want to use, so you
want to know what to get NOW that will most improve your chances to
survive.

> Late-game, spellbook of polymorph is a high-priority wish for a
spellcaster.

Wizards are really the only class that can easily and reliably cast
polymorph -- and they can write it with a magic marker fairly easily by
the time they're high enough level to cast it.  As per your later
suggestion (if it can be done in less than 100 marker charges...) this is
an awful wish.  Also, a late-game spellcaster can spend all the time in
the world hanging out at altars fishing for spellbooks.

> I think 2 blessed potions of gain ability is a horrible wish since you
can
> get them from alchemy fairly easily.

Potions of full healing and gain energy / level aren't exactly easy to
get.  It certainly isn't a high priority wish, but it's not a "horrible"
one if your stats (especially int) need improvement right away.

> Magicbane is worth enchanting over +2, since it boosts damage.

Magicbane is worthwhile at +2 and +7 only, and I'd be far more inclined to
stick with +2, especially for a wish.  If you get it at +3 you'll need
several scrolls (including cursed) to bring it up to +7, since you can't
engrave it down from +6.

I won't bother starting a holy war over this, though.  Suffice it to say,
there are whole spoilers devoted to this subject, and your suggestion is
duly noted and discarded :)

